<div class="contents usercontent">
<div class="inner">
<div class="comment-content">It's just a game.<br />Very simple game.<br />Like Linus Torvalds email:<br />On Monday, August 26, 1991 6:12:08 PM UTC+12, Linus Benedict Torvalds wrote:<br />&gt; Hello everybody out there using minix -<br />&gt;<br />&gt; I'm doing a (free) operating system (just a hobby, won't be big and<br />&gt; professional like gnu) for 386(486) AT clones. This has been brewing<br />&gt; since april, and is starting to get ready. I'd like any feedback on <br /><br />The same thing about economy.<br />Let's do it as a hobby from scratch.<br />From the elementary mathematics and algorithm theory.<br />Let's review the gold usage in the economy.<br /><br />And let's try to understand this question:<br />So how to answer on our question about how to compare garbage production if you don't see<br />garbage and don't have gold money to calculate it?<br /><br />Just believe other people.<br />But this just move this question to other people.<br />How he is comparing garbage?<br /><br />Do it from scratch and verify all the steps.<br />If it is not clear does your economy work or not compared to DIY discrete logic computer<br />makes this question even harder. Debug all the steps and write all the proofs by yourself.<div class='edittime'><em>Edited <span class="datetime"><span class="comment-date-text"> </span> <span title="">2026-07-16 06:51 (UTC)</span></span></em></div></div></div>
